 "narrative": "Compared to last report, all reported hay sales mostly steady.  Demand was moderate. Rain showers in some areas of the state has allowed pastures to green up and grow. Some pastures are probably in better shape now than this summer and some livestock are out grazing grass pastures as corn stalks are not available.  Per NASS, corn harvest in NE is at 66 percent, Soybeans at 84 percent.   Some producers are hoping for dry weather to allow the rest of the fall crops to be harvested and to bail cornstalk residue.  Cornstalk residue is a valuable feed for may feedlot to add cheap roughage to the feed ration.    Some thoughts and concern on what hay may be available to purchase after the first of the year.",
